{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a per-user feed limit (`max_feeds`, 0 = unlimited). Build and existing tests pass; the new behaviour is not covered by any test I could run.\n\n- **Schema and model:** new migration adds `users.max_feeds int not null default 0`; the field is read and written by all user queries and exposed as `max_feeds` on the user object (also added to the Go client's `User` and `UserModificationRequest`).\n- **Who can change it:** `PUT /v1/users/{userID}` accepts `max_feeds` from administrators only. A non-admin sending the field gets 403, even for their own account; a negative value gets 400.\n- **Enforcement:** the limit is checked inside `Storage.CreateFeed`, in the same transaction as the insert and with the user row locked, so every creation path (API, UI, OPML import, Google Reader API) is covered and concurrent requests cannot exceed the limit.\n- **`POST /v1/feeds`:** returns 400 and creates nothing when the user is at the limit; it is checked before fetching the remote feed and again at insert.\n- **`POST /v1/import`:** imports feeds until the limit is reached, then stops and returns 400. Feeds imported before that point are kept, so an over-sized OPML file yields a partial import plus an error rather than all-or-nothing.\n\nNot done: no new translation key was added, so the limit error is shown as a plain English message, and in the UI subscription-discovery path it surfaces as a generic database error. The Google Reader API path was not given a specific status code for this error.", "t": 1794462832.165}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794462832.165}
